  "reasoning": "For the 2026 U.S. Senate race in Nebraska, Republican incumbent Pete Ricketts is facing independent Dan Osborn; recent polling through July 6, 2026 shows a weighted average of 48.4% for Ricketts to 43.7% for Osborn, a Republican lead of 4.7 points across five polls.[12] Major forecasters (Cook, Sabato, Inside Elections) are described as rating the race \"Likely Republican,\" and a synthesized forecast notes a polling average of Ricketts +4.7, a prior 2024 contest where the same challenger lost by 6.7 points, and substantial cash and structural advantages in this historically red state.[4][10] Nebraska\u2019s statewide Cook Partisan Voting Index is R+10, indicating a strong underlying Republican lean in federal elections that aligns with both recent presidential results and the current Senate polling.[1]",
